    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/4/6/46698.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 15,
    "turn_text": "Well, the Chattanooga way is that we create a bold vision, and then we put the pieces in place and actually make it happen. It makes us very distinct from other communities. And that ebbs and flows. We go through periods of time when we're really ambitious and big things are done. We go through periods of time when that's not the case. But people, I think here, have a heart and soul that's very different than most communities and have had the ability to pull together. I mean, during those days, we sure we did the 21st century waterfront during that period of time, which I didn't even campaign on. I",
