    "turn_text": "Well, I think in business too. I mean, I don't know how many hundreds and hundreds and hundreds of contracts that, you know, negotiate around the country to build shopping centers or whatever. I don't, you know, in every case, it's got to work for both sides. And, in fact, I would say, generally speaking, business people, who go to serve in the public arena, you carry with them the trait of understanding that it's got to work for both sides or every side or it's not going to work. And so, but yeah, I mean, look, I'm used to working in a community, the mayor's office is not a partisan job. It's a job where you, again, it create a vision. You put first things first, you work with others to make that happen, and that's what we've attempted to do in the Senate.",
