    "turn_text": "No, it was exactly around. It tried to build on the successes that we had had here. But also alleviate some of the problems. I mean, you have to show metrics. Any US dollars that go into it have to be matched two to one by foreign governments and three to one by the private sector. So we set up a 501c3 in the District of Columbia. It'll end up having international board members on it, but its goal will be to end modern slavery and it has to show You have to measure how much is taking place and then show metrics as to your results and I think it's, you know, we're on the way. I mean, we've had some appropriations but what we haven't had is what's called an authorization",
