    "turn_idx": 59,
    "turn_text": "We have. I mean, again, we just got authorized 10 days ago, but there have been preliminary meetings with countries in Europe. When we were at the World Economic Forum last year, I can't in my official capacity actually ask people for money when I'm traveling as a U.S. Senator, but we met with billionaires from around the world who have an interest in this, and we met with countries that have efforts underway in their own countries. I mean what is amazing is Interpol, I mean there's all kinds of entities around the world that are involved in this, but there's not an entity that's pulling together best practices of these entities and coordinating and making sure that again we've got a goal not just to work against it. but to end it. And so I really do believe that now the hard work begins. I mean passing the bill is hard, unbelievably hard, hard to understand that a bill to end monetary slavery could be this hard to pass but it was for lots of reasons. But now the hard work begins.",
